  "verdict": "Channel 4 is not an independent probe of grey absorbers. 99.99% of the headline faint-secondary subset carries a primary mass imported from the primary's own absolute G magnitude rather than solved from the orbit - an SB1 mass function and an astrometric mass-ratio function each give one equation in two unknowns, so m1 cannot come from the orbit at all. The estimator therefore regresses absolute G on a function of absolute G, and a grey dimming slides the star along the relation instead of off it. Injection recovers +0.295 mag of residual per magnitude injected against +1.000 for the dynamical-m1 positive control, and the recovered signal saturates at 0.54 mag - below the 1.44 mag threshold the channel needs to clear - then reverses sign, so a heavily harvested star is reported as slightly OVER-luminous. The channel does not reach its own threshold at any covering fraction up to f = 1, its zero positives are uninformative, and the grey blind spot the report says only channel 4 covers is open. The headline p_total is unaffected: channel 4 does not enter the joint constraint. What is lost is coverage, and specifically the only coverage claimed for alpha = 0."
}